{"root":{"children":[{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Sending emails programmatically is a common feature in modern web applications, whether for user verification, password resets, or notifications. In Node.js, ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Nodemailer","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" is the go-to package for sending emails via any SMTP server, including Gmail, Outlook, and custom mail servers.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"As your application grows, scalability becomes a concern. While Gmail or Outlook SMTP servers work for small projects, you may need more robust email solutions like Amazon SES (Simple Email Service) for high-volume email sending.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"This guide covers how to configure Nodemailer, use environment variables for secure credentials, send emails with HTML templates, and scale with Amazon SES.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Setting Up Nodemailer in Node.js","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"extended-heading","version":1,"tag":"h2"},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"To start, you'll need to install the required packages. In this example, we’ll be using ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"dotenv","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","s